From 5f7f70211a68cbdf5d66baee4038717991273378 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GibaxLeGrand <48137851+GibaxLeGrand@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 13:44:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Launcher: Tournament Edition in the Online/LAN room (the
 game, its version, a start state per game)

The Online/LAN play window chooses the game of the matches (Sonic Riders or Sonic Riders Tournament
Edition, the extracted ones), each with its own start state (online.ini: game=, start_state= for
Sonic Riders, start_state_GXSRTE=). Room protocol SRNP-ONLINE-3: JOIN and MEMBERS carry the game's
disc ID and its main.dol's fingerprint (the runner's addresses are those of one version of TE,
2.4.6.1); the room shows OTHER GAME / OTHER GAME VERSION and the host can't start until everyone
has the host's. The match starts the room's game, whatever PLAY would start; the labels mod
(srnp_etiquettes, the US game's GTSE) is never turned on for TE; the mods' fingerprint counts the
match game's mods only; the player's GameSettings\*.ini go into the match's user folder.
PrepareGameFolder: probes of folders that may be missing (Load) have their own error code (with
the labels mod off, a missing Load folder left the error set and the game did not start). A game
that does not start says why on the launcher's output.

Measured 2026-11-26 (two launchers, TE, runner of work\te\runner, native module): both games
started from the room, waiting screen, 2228 frames of lockstep, 34 identical checksums, 0
divergences.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
